      "writtenOn": "2024-07-03T11:55:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is a really good question! I think that that is pretty compelling. It\u0027s a little ambiguous from my POV though because we do have the general concept of whether a sampler is a YCbCr sampler as part of SamplerBase. We should definitely add hashing of `mIsYCbCr` at the SamplerBase level in any case.\n\nLower-level question: How were you envisioning this working on a technical level? The current code structure of ComputeContentHash (taking in an arbitrary sequence of arbritrarily-typed arguments and computing/storing the hash once on all those arguments) would need extension in one way or another, unless there\u0027s something that I\u0027m missing.",
